{
  "title": "Third declension: consonant stems",
  "note": "Third-declension nouns show their stem in the genitive, so learn each with it: σάρξ, σαρκός (stem σαρκ-). Endings: singular -, -ος, -ι, -α or -ν; plural -ες, -ων, -σι(ν), -ας. Neuters have nominative = accusative and plural -α: σῶμα, σώματος, σώματα. Before σ, κ γ χ give ξ, π β φ give ψ, and τ δ θ drop out: σαρξί(ν), ἐλπίσι(ν).",
